# Allowlist: everything is ignored except what the image is built from, so
# docs, tools, scratch files and the like never invalidate the build cache or
# bloat the build context.  Add a line here when the Dockerfile COPYs
# something new.
*

# The Rust workspace.  dune-tool (the native dev tool) is a workspace member,
# so cargo needs its manifest, but not its source: the Dockerfile stubs it.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates/dune/Cargo.toml
!crates/dune/src/
!crates/dune-web/Cargo.toml
!crates/dune-web/src/
!crates/dune-tool/Cargo.toml

# The site, the game data it serves, and the web server's config.
!web/index.html
!web/main.js
!web/data/

!deploy/httpd.conf
